1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:02,980
SFT.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:03,980
DPO.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:04,980
PPO.

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,370
GRPO.

5
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:07,812
Distillation.

6
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:09,968
Dozens of frameworks.

7
00:00:09,988 --> 00:00:11,379
Hundreds of knobs.

8
00:00:11,399 --> 00:00:14,237
One question: how do the pieces fit together?

9
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:18,513
Underneath, it is one gradient.

10
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:20,607
μ is where the data comes from.

11
00:00:20,627 --> 00:00:22,821
ψ is how each token is weighted.

12
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:27,955
Fix the data, and it is a trainer problem.

13
00:00:27,975 --> 00:00:32,491
Let the policy generate its own data, and it becomes a systems problem.

14
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,302
That system has six layers,

15
00:00:35,322 --> 00:00:38,092
and one rule: one component per role.

16
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:42,498
Every layer has its arithmetic.

17
00:00:42,518 --> 00:00:45,612
LoRA trains about 0.4% of the weights.

18
00:00:45,632 --> 00:00:50,974
ZeRO-3 takes per-GPU memory from 120 GB to under 2.

19
00:00:52,450 --> 00:00:57,040
Online, the loop is the system: generate, score, update, sync, repeat.

20
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:58,759
Find the bottleneck first.

21
00:00:58,779 --> 00:01:03,863
One weight-transfer redesign cut that phase from 53 seconds to 7.

22
00:01:05,450 --> 00:01:07,889
Frameworks really differ in three places:

23
00:01:07,909 --> 00:01:08,940
asynchrony,

24
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,724
train–inference consistency,

25
00:01:10,744 --> 00:01:13,201
and how much of the algorithm you can own.

26
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:19,292
Look closer: every framework is a recipe of the same atoms.

27
00:01:19,312 --> 00:01:22,438
Every term of the objective has an address in the code.

28
00:01:22,458 --> 00:01:24,550
Know how deep your change must dig.

29
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,480
verl.

30
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,980
OpenRLHF.

31
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,980
slime.

32
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:31,980
SkyRL.

33
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:32,980
AReaL.

34
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:33,980
NeMo RL.

35
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,492
Each one, a different set of trade-offs.

36
00:01:39,450 --> 00:01:40,756
So: own the math.

37
00:01:40,776 --> 00:01:42,336
Reuse the runtime.

38
00:01:44,450 --> 00:01:47,051
Post-Training Systems, Layer by Layer.

39
00:01:47,071 --> 00:01:50,017
The full deep dive, in English and Chinese.

